C1: Names the owner — the role or seat that acts on this change — and that seat exists today
C2: Amends rather than contradicts: it cites the text or ruling it replaces, or says explicitly that it is new
C3: Says how we will know it worked: a check, a date, or a trigger, and who reads it
C4: Says how it is undone if it is wrong, and that undo needs no new permission
C5: States its cost (Claude budget, box/GPU hours, operator minutes) and the cost is proportionate to the change
C6: Names any single point of failure it creates and what happens when that box, lane or key is down
C7: Asks the operator only where the operator's authority is required; it does not spend attention it could avoid
C8: Does what it says and nothing more: no second change riding along with the one it claims to make
